+- PASS: fresh Windows x64 and Apple Silicon ARM64 native builds and tests; the Mac native suite ran 141 tests with zero failures. The Mac JNI library links only to operating-system libraries, with libc++ statically bundled.
+- PASS: NeoForge `test` ran 600 cases with zero failures/errors and 9 skipped; `portableTest` ran 8 with zero failures/errors. `check`, `shadowJar`, built-in model indexing and full materialization also passed; the index contains 27 models, including the default proof.
+- PASS: malformed top-level, nested and packed Protobuf geometry is rejected before native decoding. The prior Apple Silicon process-abort regression is covered by C++ and Java/JNI tests.
+- NOT TESTED: opening Minecraft on a physical Apple Silicon Mac; Microsoft account flow; model selection and rendering in a world; Iris/Distant Horizons; live-server join/synchronization; sustained gameplay. Automated CI does not establish those outcomes.
+- The local Windows account previously could not run four symbolic-link security tests because it lacked the required privilege; the same full Java suite passed on the macOS CI runner. No test was disabled.
+- A physical Apple Silicon Minecraft session, Microsoft account flow, actual model rendering/animation, Iris/Distant Horizons, multiplayer synchronization and live-server connection remain untested. The artifact is not accepted for production or release.
